WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.610
Five weird website moments. Five questions.

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:10.630
Every answer comes from a test in the repository.

3
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:18.890
Q1. Pay tapped once, reply lost, retry with the same ticket number.

4
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:26.470
How many orders exist afterwards? A: one. B: two. C: three.

5
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:37.500
A: one order. The same ticket returns the saved order.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.530
Without a ticket, the same test made two. Episode 15.

7
00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:49.130
Q2. New version published, open tab still shows Build 1.

8
00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:59.040
What happens to Build 2? A: replaces at once. B: installs and waits. C: deleted.

9
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.750
B: it installs and waits behind Build 1.

10
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:16.460
A model, not a browser recording. Episode 12.

11
00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.770
Q3. Alice loads her dashboard, then Bob loads his.

12
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:30.030
In the flawed test, what does Bob see? A: Bob. B: error. C: Alice.

13
00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.270
C: Welcome back, Alice.

14
00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:44.440
The saved page had no person in its label. Episode 24.

15
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:51.850
Q4. A deadline of January 15 shown on a New York clock.

16
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:59.270
Which date appears? A: Jan 15. B: Jan 16. C: Jan 14.

17
00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:13.310
C: January 14. Midnight in London is 7 pm the day before in New York.

18
00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.380
Episode 22.

19
00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:21.030
Q5. Contact c_1003 deleted. A direct lookup says not found.

20
00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:29.670
A search for Dana returns? A: still listed. B: nothing. C: an error.

21
00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.770
A: the contact is still listed.

22
00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:43.410
The delete removed only the main record. Episode 21.

23
00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.700
Five weird moments, each tested on a laptop.

24
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.410
Run the tests yourself. The repository is linked below.
